# 0008. Look: tokyonight tuned to the archminimal palette

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

## Context
The editor should look like the rest of the archminimal desktop (zsh prompt, tmux, terminal).

## Decision
tokyonight (moon) with overrides in `on_highlights`: one cyan accent `#00e5ff`, transparent
backgrounds, rounded borders, dim chrome. Palette values are locals at the top of
`lua/plugins/ui.lua` and are reused; a new plugin's highlights go in `on_highlights`.
The start screen and statusline show the running OS's logo, as the zsh prompt does.

## Alternatives
Not recorded at the time.

## Rationale
One accent and quiet chrome keep attention on the code and match the desktop.

## Consequences
- New UI must reuse the palette locals instead of introducing colours.

## References
- `lua/plugins/ui.lua`, README "Design pass", commit `3f6575f`
